          "description": "EMS events reported by the selected clusters over the dashboard time range. Each row is one distinct event.\n\nAn event raised before the selected time range and resolved within it shows as a Resolved row here, but is not counted in the tiles or summary tables, which count only events raised in the range.\n\n#### Panel Columns:\n\n- **Datacenter**: Datacenter of the cluster, as configured in `harvest.yml`.\n- **Cluster**: The cluster that logged the event.\n- **Node**: The node that logged the event.\n- **Message**: The EMS message name. Click it to open its description in the NetApp syslog translator.\n- **Severity**: The EMS severity (emergency, alert, error, notice, informational).\n- **Status**: Raised, or Resolved once the resolving event arrived or Harvest auto-resolved the event after its `resolve_after` time. Only bookend events (for example LUN.offline) are ever resolved; one-off events stay Raised.\n- **Details**: The event-specific fields exported for this event in the EMS collector template, for example `cache_cluster_uuid`, `cache_svm_uuid` and `revoke_type` for `flexcache.revoke.csm.failure`. Empty when the event exports no extra fields.\n",
